WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.988 --> 00:00:04.411
The next morning Ben floated into the kitchen.

2
00:00:04.491 --> 00:00:06.573
"You slept late today," Dad said.

3
00:00:06.593 --> 00:00:06.933
"Doing okay?"

4
00:00:06.953 --> 00:00:07.494
Ben shuddered.

5
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:32.124
"I had a nightmare that the bruised blue roses attacked Victoria during the wedding ceremony."

6
00:00:32.144 --> 00:00:36.708
"Good thing it was only a dream," Mom said.

7
00:00:36.728 --> 00:00:39.650
"You should have some breakfast before you leave for the garden."

8
00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:42.633
Ben hung his head.

9
00:00:42.653 --> 00:00:44.854
"What's the point of working on the garden?

10
00:00:45.455 --> 00:00:49.819
There's no singer for the wedding, no one to officiate, and the garden is a mess.

11
00:00:49.959 --> 00:00:50.899
It's a disaster!"

12
00:00:50.919 --> 00:00:52.881
"Not anymore!"

13
00:00:53.301 --> 00:00:56.144
Uncle Bert burst into the kitchen with a wide grin.

14
00:00:56.952 --> 00:00:59.114
"I have the answer to our problems!"

15
00:00:59.955 --> 00:01:03.538
Mom looked as surprised by Bert's happy expression as Ben was.

16
00:01:04.518 --> 00:01:05.099
"What is it?"

17
00:01:05.559 --> 00:01:06.120
she asked.

18
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.183
"I figured it out when I went to buy gecko food to bring to Mrs.

19
00:01:10.223 --> 00:01:12.065
Hubbletree," Uncle Bert said.

20
00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:15.868
"The pet shop owner was replacing the shop window.

21
00:01:16.268 --> 00:01:17.849
It had a large crack in it."

22
00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:22.033
"I don't understand," Ben said.

23
00:01:22.053 --> 00:01:24.375
"Do you remember when Mrs.

24
00:01:24.395 --> 00:01:25.536
Hubbletree screamed?"

25
00:01:25.928 --> 00:01:27.028
Uncle Bert asked.

26
00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:28.689
"How could I forget?"

27
00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:30.409
Ben covered his ears.

28
00:01:30.429 --> 00:01:31.950
"My head's still ringing."

29
00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:35.110
"Exactly!" Uncle Bert said.

30
00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.212
"She screamed so high the glass cracked.

31
00:01:40.352 --> 00:01:45.493
The only way to do that is to hit a high C note."

32
00:01:46.113 --> 00:01:47.094
"Uh okay."

33
00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.734
Ben was even more confused now.

34
00:01:49.754 --> 00:01:54.796
"Only a trained opera singer can hit a high C like that."

35
00:01:56.156 --> 00:01:57.397
Uncle Bert laughed.

36
00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.218
"So, I called Mrs.

37
00:02:00.258 --> 00:02:03.859
Hubbletree and asked if she would do us the honor of singing at the wedding."

38
00:02:03.879 --> 00:02:08.841
"Oh!" Ben was finally getting it.

39
00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:11.703
"And Mom asked.

40
00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:13.143
"What did she say?"

41
00:02:13.163 --> 00:02:18.826
"She said she and Mayor Hubbletree would both love to be a part of the wedding!"

42
00:02:19.246 --> 00:02:20.166
Uncle Bert said.

43
00:02:20.186 --> 00:02:25.592
"Well, after I told her we'd seat her next to Tom Ooze."

44
00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:26.292
"That's great!"

45
00:02:26.633 --> 00:02:27.293
Mom said.

46
00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.374
"I'm so relieved."

47
00:02:29.794 --> 00:02:31.275
Uncle Bert wiped his brow.

48
00:02:31.295 --> 00:02:34.656
"And now I'm off to the airport to pick up Victoria.

49
00:02:35.017 --> 00:02:35.617
See you later!"

50
00:02:36.557 --> 00:02:40.019
Cheered up by the news, Ben decided to set out for the garden.

51
00:02:40.539 --> 00:02:41.760
Then Winnie called.

52
00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.781
"Where are you?"

53
00:02:45.121 --> 00:02:45.722
she asked.

54
00:02:45.742 --> 00:02:48.623
"You need to get to the garden as fast as you can.

55
00:02:48.923 --> 00:02:50.244
There's something you need to see!"

56
00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.223
When Ben arrived at Monster Academy, Winnie was waiting for him out front.

57
00:02:58.243 --> 00:03:00.204
"What's going on?"

58
00:03:00.665 --> 00:03:03.306
Ben asked as they hurried around back to the garden.

59
00:03:03.326 --> 00:03:05.148
"Did the vines grow back?"

60
00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.129
"No, they're looking great."

61
00:03:07.149 --> 00:03:11.432
"If this is about the roses, I already know they're ruined," Ben said.

62
00:03:11.452 --> 00:03:14.514
"The roses are fine," Winnie said.

63
00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:18.276
"Waldo made more fertilizer and sprinkled it on.

64
00:03:18.757 --> 00:03:20.598
The roses are already beginning to bud."

65
00:03:20.618 --> 00:03:22.219
"Then what is it?"

66
00:03:22.439 --> 00:03:23.220
Ben asked.

67
00:03:24.921 --> 00:03:29.383
"That!" Winnie pointed to the field of black-and-orange flowers.

68
00:03:29.984 --> 00:03:33.326
For some reason, Gaby and Jen were tugging on the plants.

69
00:03:34.327 --> 00:03:35.347
Ben raced over.

70
00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.389
"What are you doing?"

71
00:03:37.929 --> 00:03:38.870
Gaby grunted.

72
00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:45.174
"Something is trying to pull them down!"

73
00:03:45.194 --> 00:03:47.656
"And it's strong!"

74
00:03:48.056 --> 00:03:48.736
Jen added.

75
00:03:49.897 --> 00:03:52.179
Ben grabbed hold of Jen and helped her tug.

76
00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:54.100
Gaby and Jen were right.

77
00:03:54.644 --> 00:03:58.527
Whatever was pulling on the flowers was strong—super strong!

78
00:03:59.027 --> 00:04:04.511
Ben and Jen held on tight, and finally their underground enemy let go.

79
00:04:04.531 --> 00:04:07.773
"What do you think is down there?"

80
00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:08.834
Ben asked.

81
00:04:09.554 --> 00:04:11.415
"We're not sure," Winnie said.

82
00:04:11.435 --> 00:04:12.756
"But come and look at this."

83
00:04:14.177 --> 00:04:15.598
Winnie showed Ben the archway.

84
00:04:16.018 --> 00:04:19.581
It was standing off-balance, one leg shorter than the others.

85
00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.382
"How did this happen?"

86
00:04:21.802 --> 00:04:22.503
Ben cried.

87
00:04:22.523 --> 00:04:25.328
"We're not sure," Winnie said.

88
00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:26.869
"But look closer."

89
00:04:28.809 --> 00:04:29.969
Ben examined the wood.

90
00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:31.890
It was covered in teeth marks.

91
00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.231
Ben was shocked.

92
00:04:34.711 --> 00:04:37.051
"Something chewed right through the wood!"

93
00:04:37.071 --> 00:04:38.972
"Do you know what this means?"

94
00:04:39.352 --> 00:04:40.152
Winnie asked.

95
00:04:40.852 --> 00:04:41.613
Ben nodded.

96
00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:44.573
"There's something around here with big teeth."

97
00:04:44.593 --> 00:04:50.215
"It means there's an explanation for all the problems we've had," Winnie said.

98
00:04:50.235 --> 00:04:52.635
"Something is causing all the trouble."

99
00:04:52.655 --> 00:04:54.376
"But what is it?"

100
00:04:54.844 --> 00:04:55.645
Ben asked.

101
00:04:55.665 --> 00:04:58.046
"Ben, come look at these!"

102
00:04:58.526 --> 00:05:00.367
Mog shouted from the piranha pond.

103
00:05:00.807 --> 00:05:07.471
Ben and the others raced over to see what Mog was staring at—large, flipper-like footprints that circled the

104
00:05:07.531 --> 00:05:11.793
pond. "What kind of creature has prints like that?"

105
00:05:12.314 --> 00:05:13.034
Ben wondered.

106
00:05:13.054 --> 00:05:19.377
"Something that likes to dig tunnels," Mog said, pointing to several deep holes nearby.

107
00:05:19.397 --> 00:05:28.619
"Okay, everybody, what kind of creature has sharp teeth, flipper-like feet, digs holes, and likes to eat flowers?"

108
00:05:29.179 --> 00:05:29.920
Ben asked.

109
00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:36.144
But before anyone could reply, Gaby let out a shout from the grassy field near the woods.

110
00:05:36.164 --> 00:05:38.546
"Everyone, come here, quick!"

111
00:05:41.628 --> 00:05:46.471
Ben didn't see anything at first, just a mud-covered lump in the middle of the field.

112
00:05:47.031 --> 00:05:51.014
But then that lump started running really fast toward the trees.

113
00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:53.596
"It's a garden gremlin!"

114
00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:54.981
Jen exclaimed.

115
00:05:55.001 --> 00:05:59.205
"Quick," Ben cried as he raced after the gremlin.

116
00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:01.247
"We have to catch him!"

117
00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:03.589
Ben and his friends took off.

118
00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:07.873
But the garden critter was much too fast.

119
00:06:08.353 --> 00:06:13.958
Not even Gaby, running as fast as she could on her long giant legs, could catch him before

120
00:06:13.998 --> 00:06:15.620
he disappeared into the woods.
